From bef7b9f5ebf13b704ea3f9ab064a510373b2df0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreamstone Ruination <claude@example.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 13:56:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Frigibax line custom shiny palettes (Dreamstone Ruination
 starters)

Replaces the canonical shiny palettes for the Frigibax evolution line with
the Cormorian heraldic identity: charcoal body with imperial gold accents
and royal blue claws/eyes. This is one of three starter palette sets for
the project (Frigibax, Teddiursa, Tinkatink); Teddiursa and Tinkatink lines
to follow in subsequent patches.

Files modified:
  graphics/pokemon/frigibax/shiny.pal
  graphics/pokemon/frigibax/overworld_shiny.pal
  graphics/pokemon/arctibax/shiny.pal
  graphics/pokemon/arctibax/overworld_shiny.pal
  graphics/pokemon/baxcalibur/shiny.pal
  graphics/pokemon/baxcalibur/overworld_shiny.pal

Approach (per DREAMSTONE_HANDOFF.md):
- Per-index sprite analysis (which palette indices control which body parts)
- Intentional color assignment per index, not auto-luminance recolor
- Front and overworld palettes analyzed separately (different index meanings)
- All RGB values are GBA-safe multiples of 8 for accurate preview-to-render fidelity
- Heraldic identity uses a consistent color set across all three species

Color identity (all values multiples of 8):
- Imperial gold bright: (248, 240, 128) - crests, beaks, belly armor highlights
- Imperial gold shadow: (176, 128, 72) - depth and shading on gold areas
- Royal blue bright: (56, 104, 248) - eyes, claws, prominent accents
- Royal blue shadow: (0, 8, 144) - depth on blue accents
- Royal blue deep: (0, 0, 64) - deepest blue shadow tones
- Charcoal mid: (72, 72, 80) - main body tone
- Charcoal dark: (40, 40, 48) - body shadows
- Charcoal deep: (24, 24, 32) - deepest body shadow
- Charcoal light: (112, 112, 120) - body highlights

Verification:
1. Apply patch in GenSpark
2. Delete any stale compiled binaries (per handoff doc): in graphics/pokemon/
   frigibax/, arctibax/, baxcalibur/ directories, delete shiny.gbapal,
   shiny.gbapal.lz, overworld_shiny.gbapal, overworld_shiny.gbapal.lz if
   present (the build will regenerate them)
3. Compile
4. Encounter or generate shiny Frigibax / Arctibax / Baxcalibur to verify
   the heraldic color identity appears as designed
